# S1A local development. Non-production. No real credentials belong in this file
# or in any file in this repository.
ACOS_CONTROL_PG_URL=postgres://acos:acos_local_dev@localhost:55432/acos_control
ACOS_AUDIT_PG_URL=postgres://acos:acos_local_dev@localhost:55433/acos_audit

# S1G. The AUDIT plane's own roles, created by `src/audit/db/migrations/A0001__audit_store.sql`
# on the audit server. They are DERIVED from ACOS_AUDIT_PG_URL by `src/audit/db/auditPool.ts`
# — the control plane never connects to the audit store as the owner:
#
#   acos_audit_replication / acos_audit_repl_dev   INSERT only. What the CONTROL plane holds.
#   acos_audit_evaluator   / acos_audit_eval_dev   Reads holdings, writes findings.
#
# ACOS_AUDIT_PG_URL above is the OWNER credential and is used for MIGRATIONS ONLY.
#
# `30 §5` requires the production audit store to be "a distinct database instance on a
# different provider or, at minimum, a separate account with a separate payment method and
# separate operator credentials". Two local containers are NOT that. See docker-compose.yml.
